  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Sulfur dioxide gas turns acidified&nbsp;potassium dichromate (VI) solution from orange to green.&nbsp;Chromium is reduced from (VI) to (III) after reaction.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>dil</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><munderover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mi>dil</mi></munderover><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Hence, On treating a compound with warm dil. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is evolved which turns <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;paper acidified with dil. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> to a green compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> respectively are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.</p>",
